  "body": "## What happens\n\nA user opened the tool editor in a build of `main` at `4d891498e`. The 3D preview draws a thread mill as a large plain cylinder. It shows no thread form, no neck and no cutting diameter that is smaller than the body. The preview does not show the tool that the user stated.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe 3D preview draws the thread mill from its stated values: the cutting diameter, the form length, the neck and the shank. The preview of a single-form or multi-form thread mill shows the thread teeth (or a band that marks them).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Reported by the user in chat on 2026-11-27 while testing the tool library refit (U8 to U12, #3663).\n- The helical flutes of #3908 work for basic end mills. Related, but a different scope: #986 (simulate and draw the thread form in the simulation).\n\n## Done means\n\n- The 3D preview of a thread mill matches its stated geometry, and a test pins the profile (for example: the cutting diameter and the neck diameter of the revolved profile).\n- No change to toolpath, simulation or posted output (display only).\n",
